@startuml
title IAbility — referenced by PokemonCard, previously undrawn

skinparam linetype ortho

interface IAbility <<sealed>> {
    - name: String
    - description: String
}

/'
  The player spends part of their turn to use it. Surfaced by
  TurnEngine.legalActions as a UseAbilityAction. See IAction.puml.
'/
class ActivatedAbility <<record>> implements IAbility {
    - action: IAction
    - oncePerTurn: boolean
    - usableWhen: ICondition<ResolutionContext>
}

/'
  Always on. Implemented entirely as triggers, exactly like ToolCard and
  StadiumCard, so nothing new is needed to dispatch them: TriggerDispatcher.collect
  walks abilities on the board along with everything else. See ITrigger.puml.
'/
class PassiveAbility <<record>> implements IAbility {
    - triggers: List<ITrigger>
    - rule: Optional<IRule>
}

/'
  Passives that are read, not fired: they must hold at every moment, through
  benching, evolving and switching mid-turn. Side.standingRules walks the board on
  each call and pairs each rule with its holder (Side.HeldRule); each rule is
  read by exactly one place in the engine, except StatusImmunity's two.
'/
interface IRule <<sealed>>

class EnergyBoost <<record>> implements IRule {
    - type: Type
    - appliesTo: ICondition<PokemonInPlay>
    - provides: int
}
note bottom of EnergyBoost : read by PokemonInPlay.providedEnergy

class EvolutionLock <<record>> implements IRule {
    - appliesTo: ICondition<PokemonInPlay>
}
note bottom of EvolutionLock : read by EvolveAction.isLegal

class NoRetreatCost <<record>> implements IRule {
    - retreating: Optional<ICondition<? super PokemonInPlay>>
    - whileHolder: ICondition<PokemonInPlay>
}
note bottom of NoRetreatCost : read by RetreatAction; the holder's own cost,
or another's when retreating is set (Tatsugiri)

class RetreatCostReduction <<record>> implements IRule {
    - amount: int
    - retreating: ICondition<? super PokemonInPlay>
    - whileHolder: ICondition<PokemonInPlay>
}
note bottom of RetreatCostReduction : read by RetreatAction; helps another Pokemon, and holders stack. Sky Support

class AttackCostReduction <<record>> implements IRule {
    - colorless: int
    - whileHolder: ICondition<PokemonInPlay>
}
note bottom of AttackCostReduction : read by Action.isLegal; only the holder's own attacks. Vigor Link (Colorless), En-fruits-iastic (Grass)

class HpBonus <<record>> implements IRule {
    - amount: int
    - holder: ICondition<PokemonInPlay>
}
note bottom of HpBonus : carried by a ToolCard, read by PokemonInPlay.maxHp

class SupporterLock <<record>> implements IRule {
    - whileHolder: ICondition<PokemonInPlay>
}
note bottom of SupporterLock : read by PlayCardAction.isLegal; the condition is on the holder

class AttackCostIncrease <<record>> implements IRule {
    - colorless: int
    - whileHolder: ICondition<PokemonInPlay>
}
note bottom of AttackCostIncrease : read by Action.isLegal; the condition is on the holder

class HealBlock <<record>> implements IRule {
}
note bottom of HealBlock : read by ResolutionContext.healingBlocked; covers both sides

class ReturnToHandWhenKnockedOut <<record>> implements IRule {}
note bottom of ReturnToHandWhenKnockedOut : carried by a ToolCard, read by TurnEngine.leavePlay
class StatusImmunity <<record>> implements IRule {
    - protects: ICondition<? super PokemonInPlay>
}
note bottom of StatusImmunity : read by AddStatus (refuses) and Side.recoverProtected (clears, after each action)

ActivatedAbility *-- IAction
PassiveAbility *-- ITrigger
PassiveAbility *-- IRule

note bottom of PassiveAbility
  Both kinds need to know which Pokemon they belong to
  ("this Pokemon takes 20 less damage"). That is the `Self`
  target, resolved through ResolutionContext.source — the
  ability is evaluated with the holder as the source.
end note

class EvolvesAs <<record>> implements IRule {
    - species: String
}
note bottom of EvolvesAs : read by EvolveAction.isLegal

@enduml
